[189.497511, "o", "  problem: Show that the planes $2x + 3y - 4z + 1 = 0$ and $5x - 2y + z + 6 = 0$ are mutually perpendicular.\r\n  deepseek_reasoning: Okay, let's see. The problem is to show that the two planes given by the equations 2x + 3y - 4z + 1 = 0 and 5x - 2y + z + 6 = 0 are mutually perpendicular. Hmm, right. So I need to figure out how to d...\r\n"]
[189.497559, "o", "  deepseek_solution: To determine if the planes \\(2x + 3y - 4z + 1 = 0\\) and \\(5x - 2y + z + 6 = 0\\) are mutually perpendicular, follow these steps:\r\n\r\n1. **Identify Normal Vectors**:  \r\n   - The normal vector of the first p...\r\n  ground_truth_solution: \r\n**Problem 377:**\r\n\r\n1. Given planes:\r\n   \\[\r\n   2x + 3y - 4z + 1 = 0 \r\n   \\]\r\n   and\r\n   \\[\r\n   5x - 2y + z + 6 = 0\r\n   \\]\r\n\r\n2. To establish that the planes are perpendicular, we use their normal vectors.\r\n   -...\r\n  domain: math\r\n  source: numina_math\r\n"]
